qt: macOS fixes: quit cleanly, keep the bundle icon

On macOS the Qt interface runs on the main thread, inside Open(), and
quitting it deadlocked twice over:

- The quit request arrives from libvlc_Quit, through the exit handler,
  with libvlc's exit lock held. Handling it right away closed the
  windows, whose close handler calls libvlc_Quit again, which waits for
  that lock. Handle it through a queued connection instead.
- Open() held the module's lock for the whole session, and the clean-up
  after app.exec() takes it again. Release it while the session runs.

And once the interface had quit, the launcher (bin/darwinvlc.m) entered
its own main loop and waited forever: the Qt session runs inside
libvlc_add_intf, and the interface replaces the launcher's exit handler,
so nothing would stop that loop. Skip it when the application has
already run.

Also, QApplication::setWindowIcon sets the Dock icon on macOS, so the
bare cone replaced the app's icon once it started. Leave it to the
bundle there.

--- a/modules/gui/qt/qt.cpp
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/qt.cpp
@@ -487,7 +487,12 @@
 #ifdef Q_OS_MAC
     /* Run mainloop on the main thread as Cocoa requires */
     libvlc_SetExitHandler( p_intf->obj.libvlc, Abort, p_intf );
+    /* The whole Qt session runs here, not on a thread of its own, and its
+     * clean-up takes this (non-recursive) lock again once app.exec()
+     * returns: holding it throughout made every quit hang. */
+    locker.unlock();
     thread( (void *)p_intf );
+    locker.relock();
 #else
     if( vlc_clone( &p_sys->thread, thread, p_intf, VLC_THREAD_PRIORITY_LOW ) )
     {
@@ -600,10 +605,15 @@
 #endif
             QSettings::UserScope, "vlc", "vlc-qt-interface" );
 
+    /* On macOS this is the Dock icon, and it would replace the app's own
+     * (the bundle's, which the system draws with the platform's shape and
+     * materials) with the bare cone. */
+#ifndef Q_OS_MAC
     if( QDate::currentDate().dayOfYear() >= QT_XMAS_JOKE_DAY && var_InheritBool( p_intf, "qt-icon-change" ) )
         app.setWindowIcon( QIcon::fromTheme( "vlc-xmas", QIcon( ":/logo/vlc128-xmas.png" ) ) );
     else
         app.setWindowIcon( QIcon::fromTheme( "vlc", QIcon( ":/logo/vlc256.png" ) ) );
+#endif
 
     /* Initialize the Dialog Provider and the Main Input Manager */
     DialogsProvider::getInstance( p_intf );
--- a/modules/gui/qt/util/qvlcapp.hpp
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/util/qvlcapp.hpp
@@ -47,7 +47,13 @@
 public:
     QVLCApp( int & argc, char ** argv ) : QApplication( argc, argv, true )
     {
-        connect( this, &QVLCApp::quitSignal, this, &QVLCApp::doQuit );
+        /* Queued: on macOS the quit request comes from libvlc_Quit, through
+         * the exit handler, on this (the main) thread and with libvlc's exit
+         * lock held. Closing the windows from inside it asks libvlc_Quit to
+         * quit again (MainInterface::closeEvent), which then waits forever
+         * for the lock. Quit once the event loop next runs instead. */
+        connect( this, &QVLCApp::quitSignal, this, &QVLCApp::doQuit,
+                 Qt::QueuedConnection );
     }
 
     static void triggerQuit()
